From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:38:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libmediaplayerservice: make the MediaPlayerService()
 constructor public

instantiate() is the only AOSP caller of the constructor, and it
registers the new object with the real servicemanager (addService).
The app process serves media.player through its own service view
instead, so atl-media-player builds the service itself, as
instantiate() does minus addService (wrap/player.cpp in that crate).

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: a private constructor cannot be called from outside the class, and no launcher flag, loader setting or environment variable changes that. The only other route, instantiate(), would addService the object on the real servicemanager, which the app process must not write to.
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 media/libmediaplayerservice/MediaPlayerService.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/media/libmediaplayerservice/MediaPlayerService.h b/media/libmediaplayerservice/MediaPlayerService.h
index 497ef798f2f6d07ff0a49710af2095410f3e106f..8764eabaf323e0250dd669d47ec611763a2ea651 100644
--- a/media/libmediaplayerservice/MediaPlayerService.h
+++ b/media/libmediaplayerservice/MediaPlayerService.h
@@ -502,7 +502,9 @@ private:
 
 // ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
+public:
                             MediaPlayerService();
+private:
     virtual                 ~MediaPlayerService();
 
     mutable     Mutex                       mLock;
